  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nHigh pressure will remained stationed over the upper Ohio Valley\nthrough most of the this week, before pushing eastward into the\nAtlantic this weekend. Warm and sunny day are expected through\nthe week with above average daytime high temperatures. Expect a\nbig diurnal temperature change during the nighttime hours, as\nefficient radiational cooling will drop lows into the upper 20s\nto low 30s tonight and tomorrow night. Warm air advection will\nas the ridge builds Thursday will help increase afternoon \ntemperatures even more and should keep overnight lows Thursday\nnight and Friday night a few degrees warmer. Enjoy this fantastic\nstretch of dry weather and above normal temperatures to do \noutdoor work/activities.\n\nThe next potential for rain isn't expected until Sunday, but \nthere is still a lot of uncertainty with the synoptic setup this\nfar out.",
